drm: dump the FB_DAMAGE_CLIPS rect list, not just its area

Follow-on diagnostic for TODO item 9. `dmg_px` alone cannot distinguish
smithay's three "damage everything" fallbacks — each of which emits exactly
ONE rect equal to the output geometry — from its `DamageShaper` inflating a
real, scattered damage set into many rects. `PlaneDamageClips::from_damage`
(smithay efeb597, backend/drm/surface/mod.rs:68-100) copies the shaper's
output into the blob one rect for one rect, so the rect count and the rect
list read here are the damage tracker's verbatim output.

Adds `dmg_nrects=` to the `[DRMSTAT]` line and, for the first 12 presents
that damage more than 512x512 px, one self-delimiting `[DMGRECTS]` line
carrying the whole clip list.

APPLY ON TOP OF: notes/m9-fb-damage-clips/fb_damage_worktree_20260806.patch
(this patch does not apply to a clean tree; it needs that one first).
Touches drivers/src/drm_device_interface.rs only, entirely behind DRM_STATS.
Builds clean: cargo build --release -p drivers --target aarch64-unknown-none.

How to read the result:
  n=1, rect = (0,0,1280,800)      -> a genuine full-output fallback; reopen
                                     the buffer-age question
  n=1, full width, height 767-775 -> shaper bbox shortcut (shaper.rs:81-88);
                                     pre-shaper set is >=2 rects, one huge
  n=4..32, rects 320 px wide      -> tiled shaper (shaper.rs:186-249); read
                                     the rect list for the real regions

Mandatory analyser assertions (this instrument must fail loudly, not
plausibly):
  1. parsed `r=` tuples == n, and the `[/DMGRECTS]` sentinel is present;
     abort otherwise (a truncated serial line must not under-report)
  2. positive control: over any window with zero `evpush` delta,
     dmg_nrects - dmg_rect == 0 and dmg_px / dmg_rect == 40960 exactly.
     If idle does not reproduce, discard the motion numbers
  3. dmg_nrects >= dmg_rect always; dmg_nrects == 0 with dmg_rect > 0 means
     the counter was never wired -- hard error, not a zero

